Ok,
	I've been playing around in Wizard mode and have discovered the
following trends towards being "zapped" by the named artifacts.

Excalibur: Zaps you when you try to pick it up.  Doesn't allow you to even
	pick it up.
Mjollnir & Vorpal Blade: Zaps you the first time you try to pick it up, then
	it seems to zap you about 1 in 4 attempts to pick it up again or wield
	it.
Stormbringer: Zaps you when you try to pick it up or wield it.

	Now, the whole point of this is to prevent non-aligned characters
from using weapons which are not of their own alignment.  I mean, the
light slap on the wrist you get from using M or VB is nothing.  Stormbringer
is slightly better but still not strict enough.  Excalibur has the right
idea.
	I am assuming that the reason it was implemented was to limit
characters to less weapons.  But IMHO, regardless of your alignment, it's
almost worth it to get Vorpal Blade anyway.
	Perhaps an additional incentive to use your own aligned weapons
should be the displeasure of your god whenever you use a non-co-aligned
weapon.  Either that or have them all act like Excalibur.
	Anyone care to comment?

